## CDS views
Core Data Services — definen data model + business semantics en ABAP.

Evolución de views clásicas del DDIC (SE11). Escritos en `.ddls` con sintaxis SQL-like + annotations.

## Estructura básica
```abap
@AccessControl.authorizationCheck: #CHECK
@EndUserText.label: 'Sales Order Item'
@Analytics.dataCategory: #FACT
define view entity ZI_SalesOrderItem
  as select from vbap
  association [0..1] to ZI_SalesOrder as _Order on $projection.VbelnAuftrag = _Order.VbelnAuftrag
{
  key vbeln     as SalesDocument,
  key posnr     as SalesDocumentItem,
      matnr     as Material,
      kwmeng    as OrderQuantity,
      netwr     as NetAmount,
      waerk     as CurrencyCode,
      _Order    // navegación
}
```

## Tipos de CDS views
### Basic view
`ZI_*` — capa fundacional, casi 1:1 con tabla.

### Composite view
`ZC_*` — junta múltiples basic views con lógica business.

### Consumption view
`ZC_*` — expuesta a apps (Fiori, OData).

### Layered architecture (VDM — Virtual Data Model)
```
Basic (I_) → Composite (I_) → Consumption (C_)
```

SAP publica cientos de views I_* en S/4HANA como building blocks.

## Annotations UI para Fiori Elements

### UI.LineItem (columnas de la tabla en List Report)
```abap
@UI.lineItem: [
    { position: 10, label: 'ID Material' },
    { position: 20, label: 'Cantidad' },
    { position: 30, label: 'Precio' }
]
```

En contexto de cada field:
```abap
@UI.lineItem: [ { position: 10 } ]
Material;

@UI.lineItem: [ { position: 20 } ]
OrderQuantity;
```

### UI.HeaderInfo (título del Object Page)
```abap
@UI: {
    headerInfo: {
        typeName: 'Producto',
        typeNamePlural: 'Productos',
        title: { value: 'name' },
        description: { value: 'category' }
    }
}
```

### UI.SelectionField (filtros en List Report)
```abap
@UI.selectionField: [ { position: 10 } ]
Material;

@UI.selectionField: [ { position: 20 } ]
CurrencyCode;
```

### UI.Facet (secciones del Object Page)
```abap
@UI: {
    facet: [
        { id: 'General', purpose: #STANDARD, type: #IDENTIFICATION_REFERENCE, position: 10, label: 'General' },
        { id: 'Precios', purpose: #STANDARD, type: #FIELDGROUP_REFERENCE, position: 20, targetQualifier: 'Prices', label: 'Precios' }
    ]
}
```

### UI.Identification (fields del formulario principal)
```abap
@UI.identification: [ { position: 10 } ]
Material;

@UI.identification: [ { position: 20 } ]
Name;
```

### UI.FieldGroup (agrupaciones)
```abap
@UI.fieldGroup: [ { qualifier: 'Prices', position: 10 } ]
NetAmount;

@UI.fieldGroup: [ { qualifier: 'Prices', position: 20 } ]
CurrencyCode;
```

## Search + filter
### Full-text search
```abap
@Search.searchable: true

@Search.defaultSearchElement: true
@Search.fuzzinessThreshold: 0.8
Name,
```

App habilita botón de búsqueda que busca en fields marcados.

### Value help
```abap
@Consumption.valueHelpDefinition: [
    { entity: { name: 'ZI_Material', element: 'Material' } }
]
Material;
```

Dropdown F4 en la UI.

## Semantic annotations
### Amount + currency
```abap
@Semantics.amount.currencyCode: 'CurrencyCode'
NetAmount,

@Semantics.currencyCode: true
CurrencyCode,
```

SAPUI5 formatea automáticamente con símbolo de moneda.

### Quantity + UoM
```abap
@Semantics.quantity.unitOfMeasure: 'BaseUnit'
OrderQuantity,

@Semantics.unitOfMeasure: true
BaseUnit,
```

### Date + time
```abap
@Semantics.systemDate.createdAt: true
CreatedAt;

@Semantics.user.createdBy: true
CreatedBy;
```

## Common issues
### 'Field labels vacíos en Fiori'
- Missing `@EndUserText.label`
- O falta annotation en data element (SE11)

### 'Value help no funciona'
- CDS de value help no existe
- Field mapping wrong
- Sin activación del CDS de value help

### 'Búsqueda no encuentra'
- `@Search.searchable: true` falta en la view
- Field no marcado con `@Search.defaultSearchElement`

### 'Column no aparece'
- Missing `@UI.lineItem` con posición
- Auth impide leer field específico

## Analizador de errores
En ADT: **Extended Check** (Ctrl+F2) → warnings + errors.

## Best practices
- **Layered VDM**: Basic → Composite → Consumption
- **Annotations en Consumption view** — no en Basic (reusable)
- **Labels claros**: usar EndUserText.label en cada field
- **Naming convention**: `Z*_<Purpose>_<Object>`
- **Documentar** con `@EndUserText.quickInfo`
- **Test con Fiori Elements preview** antes de deploy
